¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHe that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much: and he that is unjust in the least is unjust also in much.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpIf therefore ye have not been faithful in the unrighteous mammon, who will commit to your trust the true riches?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkAnd if ye have not been faithful in that which is another man's, who shall give you that which is your own?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®No servant can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd the Pharisees also, who were covetous, heard all these things: and they derided him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´And he said unto them, Ye are they which justify yourselves before men; but God knoweth your hearts: for that which is highly esteemed among men is abomination in the sight of God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThe law and the prophets were until John: since that time the kingdom of God is preached, and every man presseth into it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd it is easier for heaven and earth to pass, than one tittle of the law to fail.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWhosoever putteth away his wife, and marrieth another, committeth adultery: and whosoever marrieth her that is put away from her husband committeth adultery.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjThere was a certain rich man, which was clothed in purple and fine linen, and fared sumptuously every day:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXand there was a certain beggar named Lazarus, which was laid at his gate, full of sores,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyand desiring to be fed with the crumbs which fell from the rich man's table: moreover the dogs came and licked his sores.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And it came to pass, that the beggar died, and was carried by the angels into Abraham's bosom: the rich man also died, and was buried;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiand in hell he lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Abraham afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°And he cried and said, Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water, and cool my tongue; for I am tormented in this flame.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨But Abraham said, Son, remember that thou in thy lifetime receivedst thy good things, and likewise Lazarus evil things: but now he is comforted, and thou art tormented.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And beside all this, between us and you there is a great gulf fixed: so that they which would pass from hence to you cannot; neither can they pass to us, that would come from thence.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Then he said, I pray thee therefore, father, that thou wouldest send him to my father's house:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhfor I have five brethren; that he may testify unto them, lest they also come into this place of torment.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAbraham saith unto him, They have Moses and the prophets; let them hear them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\And he said, Nay, father Abraham: but if one went unto them from the dead, they will repent.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}And he said unto him, If they hear not Moses and the prophets, neither will they be persuaded, though one rose from the dead.¦layout ªlast_verse